## Iteration

Prefer **O(n)** single passes and **index maps** over nested `for` loops.

| Pattern | Prefer |
|---------|--------|
| Find + update by ID in a list | `[ID: Int]` index map (`rowIndexByID`, `indexByID` in `TransactionStore`) |
| Filter / map / transform | `filter`, `map`, `reduce` on collections |
| Stream batches | one outer `for await` / `for in`; no inner scan of the full collection per item |
| Build index while appending | `enumerated()` once when constructing the map |

```swift
// ❌ AVOID — O(n²) scan per batch item
for transaction in batch {
    if let i = allRows.firstIndex(where: { $0.id == transaction.id }) {
        allRows[i] = rowState(for: transaction)
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD — O(1) lookup
if let i = rowIndexByID[id] {
    allRows[i] = updatedRow
}
```

**When nested loops are acceptable:** small bounded inner sets (e.g. ≤3), or a documented unavoidable cross-product — add a one-line comment explaining why.

---

## Extraction trigger

Extract a private helper when flattening would leave a function doing more than one conceptual job (e.g. "sync cache" vs "apply search visibility").
